    fields:  # 4b1c
      statement: "A catalogue row must name the boundary its call actually crosses. VIOLATED in go.yaml, three rows, two modules. os/exec [Command, CommandContext, LookPath] is rowed subprocess: LookPath loops PATH calling os.Stat and unix.Eaccess and creates no process, and CommandContext calls Command which calls LookPath and only BUILDS a *Cmd -- the process is created later, by Start(). net/http [Get, Post, PostForm, Head, NewRequest] is rowed net_send: NewRequest wraps NewRequestWithContext, which parses the URL and populates a Request struct in memory; the dial happens later in Client.Do. Two independent workers reached the same conclusion on different chunks."  # 4b1c
      root_cause: "Module-granularity attribution again, and this instance is already NAMED in the codebase: io_boundary.py, in the docstring of the function that computes INV-nular's own count, records that families of rows where the primitive does not perform the declared operation have been swept out of the VOUCHED catalogue, listing \"constructors declared net_send\" explicitly. net/http.NewRequest is that family verbatim. These rows are in the REMAINDER, which the 2026-09-06 ruling left disclosed rather than read -- so this is not a new class, it is evidence that the already-ruled classes survive in the unswept portion. NOTE: the register itself is known to be inaccurate; WI-roluz records that \"seven families\" is short by five."  # 4b1c
